<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="36e3401f">&lt;p&gt;
    One of the key steps in benefits quantification is arriving at the benefits schedule and defining the milestones for
    each benefit horizon - this will be useful for tracking the benefits. By leveraging the benefits assumptions and
    working with the operations, a benefits schedule can be developed. The schedule and related assumptions will be inputs
    to the deployment plan.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Evaluate specific changes. The evaluation should:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Assume a learning curve for realization of benefits (i.e., hypercare period, slowed workpace during adoption, etc.)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop a benefits realization curve based on timing assumptions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Include a reporting format (scorecard) to track actual change against assumed benefit capture
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
